Answer: There are two errors:
\begin{itemize}
\item `str_text` is a Python string, but `print` only prints bytes.  You'll need to convert it to bytes before printing.
\item `print` does not interpret newlines.  You'll need to add a newline to the end of the string before printing.
\end{itemize}

Use the [`bytes` module](https://docs.python.org/3/library/bytes.html) to convert the string to bytes and then the [`r` prefix](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#bytes.r) function to convert that back to a `str`.

\begin{code}
str_text = file.read()
bytes_text = str_text.encode('utf-8')
print(bytes_text.rstrip().decode('utf-8'))
\end{code}

Comment: `print` does *not* "ignore" the newline. It doesn't interpret the newline at all; it merely prints the bytes as a line on the console.

